  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 257 PM EDT Tue Oct 13 2026\n\n- Showers and isolated storms tonight\n\nA few showers and isolated thunderstorms have developed this\nevening in the far southern row of Michigan counties. This\nactivity looks to sweep east and south of the area late this\nafternoon. The reasoning for this is the front is surging in the\nsame direction and winds are becoming slightly divergent off of\nLake Michigan. \n\nWe expect additional precipitation to develop tonight however as\nthe front drifts south into Northern Indiana. Mid level shortwaves\nworking eastward through the Southern Great Lakes will interact\nwith the nearby front and showers and a few storms will develop\nafter sunset. The best chances for rain will come along the I-94\ncorridor, but we will have chance pops all the way north into the\nI-96 corridor. Rainfall will be on the light side on the order of\na tenth of an inch or less. \n\n- Showers and a few storms Thursday into Friday\n\nThe most impactful weather of the forecast period will come\nThursday into Friday as a fall system moves through the Great\nLakes. The low will be deepening as it heads east, approaching\n990mb at it moves well east of the area. Winds will increase on \nthe backside of the low on Friday with gusts over 40 mph certainly\npossible. \n\nThe system will be deepening as shortwaves from both the northern\nand southern streams phase over the Great Lakes region. The result\nis the low swinging through along with deep moisture and lift.\nRainfall will not be overly heavy with 0.25 to 0.75 inch amounts\ncommon. Some thunder is possible given the dynamic nature of the\nsystem, especially towards I-94 given surface dew points rising\nback in the lower 60s for a time. \n\nLake effect rain showers are expected on Friday along with the\ndriving northwest wind. Delta T's will push into the upper teens\non Friday. It will be a wet day along the lakeshore for this\nreason. \n\n- Temperatures up and down through the 7 day forecast\n\nTemperatures will be on a bit of a roller coaster with 60s to\naround 70 for highs tomorrow. Highs will only reach the 50s on\nFriday and Saturday given the cold air aloft. We should push back\ntowards 70 next Tuesday.",
